Let $B$ represent basketball and $V$ represent volleyball. Adding the two totals counts the overlap twice, so subtract it once.

$\begin{aligned}|B\cup V|&=|B|+|V|-|B\cap V|\\&=27+21-9\\&=39\end{aligned}$

$39$ members play basketball or volleyball.

